---
title: Final Light Resources | Questadon
description: Free extras for Final Light - character sheets and other printables for your table.
layout: layout.njk
permalink: /final-light/resources/index.html
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
# Unlisted for now: reached from the QR code in the book (via /fl), not linked
# anywhere on the site. Drop this line to let search engines find it.
noindex: true
# One entry per download. To add one, put the file in /downloads/ and add an
# entry here - the page lays itself out from this list.
resources:
  - title: Blank Character Sheet
    blurb: A fresh sheet for a new survivor. No personal stakes section.
    file: /downloads/FL-Character-Sheet-Blank.pdf
    details: PDF · 1 page · 2.4 MB
  - title: Pregen Character Sheets
    blurb: Five pre-generated characters with backgrounds and personal stakes.
    file: /downloads/FL-Character-Sheets-Pregens.pdf
    details: PDF · 5 pages · 2.7 MB
---
{# Landing page for the QR code printed in the Final Light book. The QR code
   points at /fl (fl.njk), never here, so this page can move or be renamed
   without reprinting anything. #}
<article class="prose fl-resources">
  <p class="project-page__breadcrumb"><a href="/projects/final-light-ttrpg/">&larr; Final Light</a></p>

  <header class="prose__header">
    <h1>Final Light Resources</h1>
    <p class="project-page__lead">
      Thanks for picking up Final Light. Here are some free extras for your
      table. Download whatever you need and print as many as you like.
    </p>
  </header>

  <ul class="fl-resources__list">
    {% for item in resources %}
    <li class="fl-resources__item">
      <div class="fl-resources__text">
        <h2 class="fl-resources__title">{{ item.title }}</h2>
        <p class="fl-resources__blurb">{{ item.blurb }}</p>
        <p class="fl-resources__details">{{ item.details }}</p>
      </div>
      <a class="project-page__cta fl-resources__cta" href="{{ item.file }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-resource="{{ item.file | replace('/downloads/', '') }}" aria-label="Download {{ item.title }}">Download</a>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</article>

<script>
  {# One event for every file, told apart by file_name, so new resources show
     up in GA4 without any changes here. Custom name for the same reason as
     the Quick Start page: GA4's own `file_download` also fires on these
     clicks, and keeping ours separate keeps the count clean. Files open in a
     new tab; beacon transport is a safety net for browsers that open the PDF
     in this one anyway. #}
  document.querySelectorAll('[data-resource]').forEach(function(link) {
    link.addEventListener('click', function() {
      gtag('event', 'resource_download', {
        file_name: link.dataset.resource,
        transport_type: 'beacon'
      });
    });
  });
</script>
